{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297712-new-spell-master-of-five-elements","id":1297712,"title":"New spell: Master of Five Elements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-18T07:16:07-07:00","id":1297712,"title":"New spell: Master of Five Elements","content":"<b>Master of Five Elements</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15sm, 1wp<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <br /> Twisting her hands into the Five Elemental Mudras, the sorcerers asserts her dominion over the natural forces of Creation, bending them briefly to her command. Upon casting this spell, the sorcerer should select one of the following elements, and gain those effects for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <i>Air:</i> The sorcerer can send out powerful gusts of wind, strong enough to knock an unprepared individual down, or to change the course of a ship upon the sea. She may direct this wind in combat, using her (Intelligence + Occult) to attack and treating the wind as a light thrown weapon with the Bashing, Smashing, and Flexible tags, or to deflect the weapons of her enemies, imposing a penalty of (Essence) on any ranged attacks targeting her or her allies out to short range. When used on the water, this can add or subtract up to 3 from a wind-powered vessel's Speed.<br /> <br /> <i>Earth:</i> The sorcerer can command stone to break. In areas with large amounts of stone or clay, she can break the ground beneath an enemy's feet, or crack the walls of a building or cliff. Breaking the ground is a special gambit (Difficulty 2), with an attack roll of (Wits + Occult) to knock the target prone. Regardless of the success of the gambit, this will turn the ground around him out to Close range into difficult terrain; when in a building with stone floors, it will instead simply drop everyone who cannot succeed at a reflexive (Dexterity + Athletics) check, difficulty 3, down one floor. Breaking the earth in this fashion can also be used to enhance appropriate feats of demolition and destruction, allowing the sorcerer to treat her Strength as (Essence + Intelligence) and her Athletics as (Occult). Finally, at the Storyteller's discretion, breaking the ground along a cliff face, mountain side, or in other environments where stones may simply begin to rain down could create an environmental hazard of falling rocks.<br /> <br /> <i>Fire</i>: The sorcerer commands the flame to consume or to withhold. For the remainder of the scene, the sorcerer is immune to natural flame and the consequences thereof; she will not suffer from smoke inhalation, nor will her clothing singe. Additionally, she may command sources of natural flame to explode violently; this is a special gambit (difficulty 2), targeting everyone in Close range to a natural flame. Her victims treat this as an explosive trap, with a difficulty to avoid equal to the successes on the gambit's initiative roll and damage equal to a bonfire (Exalted p 232), but without any interval. Of course, such explosions may set secondary fires that serve as their own environmental hazards.<br /> <br /> <i>Water</i>: The sorcerer commands wave and current, pushing and pulling her enemies. For the remainder of the scene, she may move through up to neck high water as normal terrain and without needing to swim. She may command the water to strike her foes down, using her (Intelligence + Occult) to attack and treating the water as a thrown weapon with the Bashing, Smashing, and Flexible tags. Enemies in knee deep or shallower water treat this as as a light thrown weapon; enemies in water up their midsection treat this as a medium thrown weapon; enemies in deeper water treat this as a heavy thrown weapon. She may also add or subtract up to 3 from the speed of any vessel on the water.<br /> <br /> <i>Wood</i>: The sorcerer can command plant life to shrink or grow. In areas with large amounts of woody vegetation or undergrowth, she may make a special grapple gambit (difficulty 2) to grapple a target at out to Short range, using her (Intelligence + Occult) for the control roll; her extra successes may only be used to restrain or savage the target, not to throw or drag them. She may also turn the terrain around one target out to Medium range into difficult terrain. In wooden buildings or other structures, she may command the wood to break; treat this like command of the Earth.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer who knows Master of the Five Elements as her control spell are treated as nobility by elementals, and may treat any elemental as having a Minor tie of respect. Such sorcerers are always surrounded by minor elemental effects; fires burn hotter and brighter in their presence, smoke bends away from them, dirt and dust does not cling to them, and thorns and vines do not catch on their clothes.<br /> <br /> <i>Distortion </i>(Goal Number: 5): You steal control of the element selected by the sorcerer, for a number of turns equal to your excess successes.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I was aiming for this to be Terrestrial Circle, but... I dunno, is this Terrestrial or Celestial?<br /> <br /> Maybe you only gain one element on learning it, and subsequent elements cost 4xp or 2bp to add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T07:57:47-07:00","id":1297722,"title":"","content":"Seems quite ok for a terrestrial. <br /> <br /> Actually, I think it should be a bit stronger. Cause when I see wood, I see mokuton, and for the other elements, I see Avatar: The last airbender. How about a dice pool based upon occult + intelligence, and you can use those pool to do actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T10:26:44-07:00","id":1297999,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the spell overall! It's definitely cool, and I really like the control spell effect. However, I think this might be a <i>bit</i> too powerful for Terrestrial Circle. Notably, several of the individual elemental effects seem to come close to other full Terrestrial Circle spells. The Air effect, for example, seems to be quite close to Calling The Wind's Kiss (I know, 2nd edition, but I'm not willing to bet it won't eventually make it into 3rd). <br /> <br /> Of course, if you bump it to Celestial Circle, I think it's then a bit weak for that. My suggestion would be to increase it to Celestial Circle, and increase it's power somewhat. I'd suggest some or all of the following:<ul><li>Allow switching between elements controlled by taking a shape sorcery action and spending 1 WP.</li> <li>Have the base effect of each element to be the ability to increase or decrease penalties from that element in some range around you (I'd say short), by up to (Essence). So if you're Essence 3, in water mode, you could cancel 3 points of penalties from heavy rain, or cause a fog to raise up and impose a -3 penalty on ranged attacks or Awareness rolls against you.</li> <li>Create some &quot;spend motes for extra effects&quot; options, similar to what Wood Dragon's Claw has. Offhand, I'd give each element the ability to create a hazard around you, that the caster's immune to but affects everyone else within close or short range to them, an &quot;elemental burst&quot; attack (similar to what you've given air and water), and possibly a unique thing for each element. I like the gambits, could one of those be provided for each element?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}